From 535487a0c539fdaf7d5e786bb52ef672426312b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shifangx <shifangx@nvidia.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 16:11:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(nemotron): serve Nemotron 3.5 Super VL, LayerNorm and
 all

Super checkpoints declare architecture NemotronH_Omni_Reasoning_V3 and
model_type nemotron_h_omni; only the Nano_ spellings were registered, so
sglang could not resolve them at all. Registering the names is most of
this commit and the least interesting part of it.

The part that matters: Super carries one weight-bearing layer the Nano
class does not have. vision_projector.vision_final_layernorm.{weight,
bias} is a LayerNorm over the RADIO features, applied before pixel
shuffle and the projector MLP. The reference implementation keys its
presence on the language model having MTP layers -- Megatron-Core
appends a final LayerNorm to every block built from a config carrying
mtp_num_layers, and the vision tower inherits that field from the LLM --
and this checkpoint has num_nextn_predict_layers: 1, so the layer is
real and its weights are in the files.

load_weights() routes by prefix through an if/elif chain with no else
branch. Registering the architecture name alone would therefore have
produced a run that starts cleanly, drops both tensors on the floor,
skips the LayerNorm, and serves wrong image embeddings with nothing in
the log. That is why NemotronH_Omni_Reasoning_V3 is a real subclass
rather than the `pass` its Nano sibling gets, and why its loader raises
when the pair is missing or renamed instead of inheriting that silence.

The seam is normalize_vision_features(), a no-op on the base class,
called from all three feature paths (dynamic-resolution, fixed-size,
video) right after the vision tower and before any reshape. LayerNorm
acts per token on the last dimension, so normalizing the packed features
there is equivalent to the reference's placement inside the projector,
and the three call sites stay a one-line change each.

The config class is a pure alias: AutoConfig.register requires
cls.model_type to equal the key it is registered under, the same
constraint that makes the DeepSeek V3.2/V4 aliases subclasses in
utils/hf_transformers/common.py.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
